  "description": "Passengers who wait too long leave (ARCHITECTURE decision 731). station-demand.json's Home (1) and Office (2), 4,096 units (64 m) apart, on line 1 Main (Home, Office) with no train, one trip a day each way; passengers' patience is turned on. As in station-demand.json, Home's one passenger for Office is released at 08:59 (minute 539) and waits for line 1 outbound. The trip is an ordinary one (not beyond the map, no high-speed line, 64 m < 20 km), so the passenger waits 40 minutes: at each whole minute t, before the minute's release, a group leaves once t - since >= 40. At 09:38 (578) it has waited 39 minutes and is still there; at 09:39 (579) it has waited 40 and leaves, counted at Home as gaveUp 1 (not abandoned), so released 1 = waiting 0 + gaveUp 1. Office's passenger is not released before 18:00, so nobody waits there. Balance 6,000 - two stations of 3,000 = 0. Every value is worked out by hand from the rule; the difference model does not hold the rule, so this fixture runs on GameCore only.",
